% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for made up textile articles, in the words of the
% tariff (Chapter 63). Each word cites the text that says what it means:
% the tariff's headings and notes, US Customs rulings, the EU explanatory
% notes to Chapter 63, a dictionary or an encyclopedia, and the description
% of the listings' fields (sources/listings/
% marketplace_fields_other_products.txt) for what a field means. Bridges.
%
% The fields read: the kind (Item Type, Type, Category, Product Type); how
% the textile is made (Technics); the material named (Material: Cloth,
% Canvas, Terry); the shop's category "Home & Garden > Home Textile".
% "Material: 100% Polyester" is a share of a fibre: the reader writes it as
% "the good contains 100 percent of polyester", and the materials
% background reads the fibre names.
%
% Left out, because no saved text says what the word means for the tariff:
%   - "mask" (a face mask of 6307, or a costume mask of Chapter 95), "cover"
%     and "car seat cover" (a furnishing of 6304, or a part of a motor
%     vehicle of heading 8708: HQ H249319), "mat" and "car mat" (a floor
%     covering of Chapter 57 or 39, a placemat of 6302);
%   - "pillow" and "cushion" (bedding of heading 9404, which the model does
%     not cover), "duvet cover", "table runner", "tapestry" (heading 5805);
%   - "Technics: Embroidered" (embroidery is in the lines below six digits)
%     and "Technics: Spray Painting" (not the printing of the fabric);
%   - "Microfiber": a synthetic fibre, but the listing does not say which.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* names the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a thing* is in the shop category *a category*.
    *a name* is a word for the textile kind *a kind*.
    *a field* is a field of the kind of a textile article.
    *a value* is a technics value for *a construction*.
    *a name* is a word for a textile fabric.
    *a name* is a word for a terry fabric.
    *a category* is a shop category of textile articles.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.
    *a good* is of textile material.
    the fabric of *a garment* is terry.

